## PySide6 — LGPL-3.0-only

Qt for Python. **LGPL-3.0-only**, which is why it was chosen over the
source-only PyGObject/GTK4 stack: an LGPL dependency is safe to redistribute in
a public repository, and PySide6 ships manylinux/win/macOS wheels while
PyGObject is source-distribution only on PyPI.

- Upstream: <https://www.qt.io/licensing/open-source-lgpl-obligations>
- Wheels are unmodified upstream binaries. Dynamically linking the LGPL
  libraries is the supported distribution mode; no LGPL source is bundled here.

## Toga — BSD-3-Clause

BeeWare Toga plus its `toga-gtk` backend. BSD-3-Clause, a permissive licence
compatible with MIT redistribution.

- Upstream: <https://github.com/beeware/toga>

## The rest

Everything else pulled in at install time keeps its own licence, including
ONNX Runtime (MIT), PyTorch (BSD-3-Clause), OpenCV (Apache-2.0), numpy
(BSD-3-Clause), spandrel (MIT), selectolax (MIT), requests (Apache-2.0) and
the model weights themselves, which keep the licences listed per entry in
`models/catalogue.json`.
